task_messages.content:
The appointment: {{ summary }}

If that starts with 'Booked:', it is already booked; never call book_offer for it. If it does not say the caller has heard the confirmation reference, tell them they are booked, read the reference one character at a time, and ask if there is anything else; otherwise answer what the caller says next. If it does not start with 'Booked:', the caller has just said yes to the read-back of exactly that appointment: call book_offer now; it takes no arguments. If it returns taken or refused, apologise briefly and pass the caller's next wish to update_request. If the caller changes the time or details before it is booked, pass that to update_request and follow its result; call book_offer again only after they say yes to its new read-back.

For a question about a location, a doctor, or whether we offer something, call lookup and answer in one sentence from its facts only. If the caller wants another appointment, call book_another. When the caller needs nothing else, call finish.
